<title>FRANCE: New York top Ex-Paris cargo destination Jan-Apr 97.</title>
<headline>New York top Ex-Paris cargo destination Jan-Apr 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in January-April 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in the first four months of 1997, with the percentage change on January-April 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    Origin			   Percent</p>
<p>			  tonnes     Change 1996</p>
<p> 1. New York	  11,457    down  4.7</p>
<p> 2. Chicago	    9108	 up 10.3</p>
<p> 3. Tokyo		8421     down 11.4</p>
<p> 4. Hong Kong	  7471	 up  6.5</p>
<p> 5. Montreal	   4506     down  6.2</p>
<p> 6. Mexico City	4330	 up 18.6</p>
<p> 7. Sao Paulo	  4315	 up 26.9</p>
<p> 8. Singapore	  3645	 up 45.1</p>
<p> 9. Los Angeles	3271     down 13.6</p>
<p> 10. Miami	     2622	 up 22.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
